<div class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap">no, no, I am running Quantize &amp; comp=
ile ONNX to zk circuit

but I am using the up-to-date ezkl. please support me for providing the cor=
rect arguments.

=E2=9C=85 Correct modern EZKL workflow (2024=E2=80=932025 versions)
Step 1 =E2=80=94 Generate settings (this performs quantization automaticall=
y)
ezkl gen-settings \
  --model circuits/age_v1/model.onnx \
  --output circuits/age_v1/settings.json


This does:

analyzes the ONNX

runs internal calibration

finds quantization scales

stores them in settings.json

=F0=9F=91=89 THIS replaces ezkl quantize.

Step 2 =E2=80=94 Compile circuit
ezkl compile-circuit \
  --model circuits/age_v1/model.onnx \
  --settings circuits/age_v1/settings.json \
  --output circuits/age_v1/circuit.ezkl


This produces:

quantized circuit graph

compiled ops

field elements

ready for prover setup

Step 3 =E2=80=94 Generate proving keys
ezkl setup \
  --settings circuits/age_v1/settings.json \
  --circuit circuits/age_v1/circuit.ezkl \
  --vk circuits/age_v1/vk.key \
  --pk circuits/age_v1/pk.key

Step 4 =E2=80=94 Produce witness (input)

Use your real miner input later. For testing:

ezkl gen-random-data \
  --model circuits/age_v1/model.onnx \
  --output circuits/age_v1/input.json


Then:

ezkl gen-witness \
  --circuit circuits/age_v1/circuit.ezkl \
  --input circuits/age_v1/input.json \
  --output circuits/age_v1/witness.json

Step 5 =E2=80=94 Prove
ezkl prove \
  --circuit circuits/age_v1/circuit.ezkl \
  --pk circuits/age_v1/pk.key \
  --witness circuits/age_v1/witness.json \
  --proof circuits/age_v1/proof.json

Step 6 =E2=80=94 Verify locally
ezkl verify \
  --proof circuits/age_v1/proof.json \
  --vk circuits/age_v1/vk.key

=E2=AD=90 FINAL NOTES
=E2=9C=94 quantize command is deprecated
=E2=9C=94 Quantization now happens inside gen-settings
=E2=9C=94 You should never call quantize manually in latest EZKL versions
=E2=9C=94 Your ONNX opset=3D18 model is fully compatible


