<hr data-start=3D"809" data-end=3D"812">
<h1 data-start=3D"814" data-end=3D"839">=E2=9D=97 Why this is required?</h1=
>
<p data-start=3D"841" data-end=3D"913">EZKL uses <strong data-start=3D"851"=
 data-end=3D"860">Tract</strong> internally.<br data-start=3D"872" data-end=
=3D"875">
Tract only supports about 25 ONNX ops.</p>
<p data-start=3D"915" data-end=3D"978">Unsupported ops that ALWAYS break EZ=
KL (freeze at translation):</p>
<ul data-start=3D"980" data-end=3D"1351">
<li data-start=3D"980" data-end=3D"1020">
<p data-start=3D"982" data-end=3D"1020">Resize (especially bicubic / biline=
ar)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1021" data-end=3D"1041">
<p data-start=3D"1023" data-end=3D"1041">Pad (mode=3Dreflect)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1042" data-end=3D"1063">
<p data-start=3D"1044" data-end=3D"1063">Softmax (sometimes)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1064" data-end=3D"1087">
<p data-start=3D"1066" data-end=3D"1087">Flatten + Dynamic ops</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1088" data-end=3D"1105">
<p data-start=3D"1090" data-end=3D"1105">ArgMax / ArgMin</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1106" data-end=3D"1142">
<p data-start=3D"1108" data-end=3D"1142">GlobalAveragePool in some versions=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1143" data-end=3D"1160">
<p data-start=3D"1145" data-end=3D"1160">Dynamic Reshape</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1161" data-end=3D"1175">
<p data-start=3D"1163" data-end=3D"1175">InstanceNorm</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1176" data-end=3D"1187">
<p data-start=3D"1178" data-end=3D"1187">LayerNorm</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1188" data-end=3D"1196">
<p data-start=3D"1190" data-end=3D"1196">Expand</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1197" data-end=3D"1207">
<p data-start=3D"1199" data-end=3D"1207">Upsample</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1208" data-end=3D"1265">
<p data-start=3D"1210" data-end=3D"1265">Dropout (should be constant-folded=
 but sometimes isn't)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1266" data-end=3D"1285">
<p data-start=3D"1268" data-end=3D"1285">NonMaxSuppression</p>
</li>
