<hr data-start=3D"720" data-end=3D"723">
<h1 data-start=3D"725" data-end=3D"774">=F0=9F=A7=A8 <strong data-start=3D"=
730" data-end=3D"774">This is a confirmed compatibility issue:</strong></h1=
>
<p data-start=3D"776" data-end=3D"889">=E2=9C=94 EZKL supports opset 18 for=
 <em data-start=3D"805" data-end=3D"811">some</em> models<br data-start=3D"=
818" data-end=3D"821">
=E2=9D=8C But NOT when PyTorch exports ReduceMean dynamically (without axes=
)</p>
<p data-start=3D"891" data-end=3D"963">The PyTorch 2.3+ ONNX exporter <stro=
ng data-start=3D"922" data-end=3D"932">always</strong> emits ReduceMean wit=
hout axes.</p>
<p data-start=3D"965" data-end=3D"975">Therefore:</p>
<h1 data-start=3D"977" data-end=3D"1036">=E2=9D=8C <strong data-start=3D"98=
1" data-end=3D"1036">PyTorch 2.3 =E2=86=92 ONNX opset 18 =E2=86=92 EZKL =3D=
 NOT COMPATIBLE</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"1038" data-end=3D"1058">You will ALWAYS get:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1060" data-end=3D"1175">
<li data-start=3D"1060" data-end=3D"1090">
<p data-start=3D"1062" data-end=3D"1090">version converter failures</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1091" data-end=3D"1123">
<p data-start=3D"1093" data-end=3D"1123">ReduceMean with missing axes</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1124" data-end=3D"1139">
<p data-start=3D"1126" data-end=3D"1139">EZKL freeze</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1140" data-end=3D"1160">
<p data-start=3D"1142" data-end=3D"1160">no settings.json</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1161" data-end=3D"1175">
<p data-start=3D"1163" data-end=3D"1175">no circuit</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1177" data-end=3D"1180">
<h1 data-start=3D"1182" data-end=3D"1214">=F0=9F=8E=AF <strong data-start=
=3D"1187" data-end=3D"1214">When can opset 18 work?</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"1216" data-end=3D"1341">Only if your model <strong data-st=
art=3D"1235" data-end=3D"1290">does NOT contain ReduceMean / ReduceSum / Re=
duceMax</strong><br data-start=3D"1290" data-end=3D"1293">
or<br data-start=3D"1295" data-end=3D"1298">
the axes are explicit in the PyTorch model.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1343" data-end=3D"1357">But even then:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1359" data-end=3D"1396">PyTorch 2.3+ ONNX exporter still:=
</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1397" data-end=3D"1556">
<li data-start=3D"1397" data-end=3D"1425">
<p data-start=3D"1399" data-end=3D"1425">ignores opset_version=3D17</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1426" data-end=3D"1445">
<p data-start=3D"1428" data-end=3D"1445">forces opset 18</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1446" data-end=3D"1494">
<p data-start=3D"1448" data-end=3D"1494">emits ops that may not be supporte=
d by Tract</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1495" data-end=3D"1556">
<p data-start=3D"1497" data-end=3D"1556">uses ONNXScript converter which is=
 NOT Tract-friendly yet</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1558" data-end=3D"1561">
<h1 data-start=3D"1563" data-end=3D"1596">=E2=AD=90 <strong data-start=3D"1=
567" data-end=3D"1596">So what are your choices?</strong></h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"1598" data-end=3D"1666">=E2=9C=94 OPTION 1 =E2=80=94 Use =
legacy PyTorch exporter (PyTorch 2.0.x / 2.1.x)</h3>
