<p data-start=3D"2005" data-end=3D"2060">This works, <strong data-start=3D"=
2017" data-end=3D"2024">BUT</strong> PyTorch opset 18 may also generate:</p=
>
<ul data-start=3D"2062" data-end=3D"2182">
<li data-start=3D"2062" data-end=3D"2073">
<p data-start=3D"2064" data-end=3D"2073">NonZero</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2074" data-end=3D"2090">
<p data-start=3D"2076" data-end=3D"2090">DynamicShape</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2091" data-end=3D"2101">
<p data-start=3D"2093" data-end=3D"2101">Expand</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2102" data-end=3D"2132">
<p data-start=3D"2104" data-end=3D"2132">Flatten with symbolic dims</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2133" data-end=3D"2150">
<p data-start=3D"2135" data-end=3D"2150">Dropout nodes</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2151" data-end=3D"2169">
<p data-start=3D"2153" data-end=3D"2169">Identity nodes</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2170" data-end=3D"2182">
<p data-start=3D"2172" data-end=3D"2182">Cast ops</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2184" data-end=3D"2212">Any of these may break EZKL.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2214" data-end=3D"2264">So patching only ReduceMean is usu=
ally not enough.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2266" data-end=3D"2335">=E2=9C=94 OPTION 3 =E2=80=94 Remo=
ve ONNXScript entirely and force legacy exporter</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2336" data-end=3D"2391">If you force the legacy exporter, =
opset 17 works again.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2393" data-end=3D"2441">But PyTorch 2.3+ removed some of t=
he legacy API.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2443" data-end=3D"2446">
<h1 data-start=3D"2448" data-end=3D"2481">=E2=AD=90 <strong data-start=3D"2=
452" data-end=3D"2481">Conclusion =E2=80=94 Final Answer</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"2483" data-end=3D"2538">=E2=9D=8C You cannot reliably use=
 opset 18 ONNX with EZKL.</h2>
<h2 data-start=3D"2539" data-end=3D"2620">=E2=9D=8C PyTorch 2.3+ ONNX expor=
t =E2=86=92 EZKL is not compatible (because of ReduceMean).</h2>
<h2 data-start=3D"2621" data-end=3D"2682">=E2=9C=94 You MUST export with op=
set 17 (using legacy exporter).</h2>
<h2 data-start=3D"2683" data-end=3D"2755">=E2=9C=94 Or downgrade to PyTorch=
 2.1.0 / 2.0.1 to restore legacy exporter.</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2757" data-end=3D"2816">This is the <strong data-start=3D"=
2769" data-end=3D"2800">only stable production path</strong> for SN2 miners=
.</p>
