<p data-start=3D"221" data-end=3D"242">This happens because:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"244" data-end=3D"411">
<li data-start=3D"244" data-end=3D"314">
<p data-start=3D"246" data-end=3D"314">PyTorch 2.0.1 + torchvision 0.15.2 a=
re built against <strong data-start=3D"299" data-end=3D"312">NumPy 1.x</str=
ong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"315" data-end=3D"366">
<p data-start=3D"317" data-end=3D"366">But your <code data-start=3D"326" da=
ta-end=3D"336">.venv310</code> currently has <strong data-start=3D"351" dat=
a-end=3D"364">NumPy 2.x</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"367" data-end=3D"411">
<p data-start=3D"369" data-end=3D"411">So torchvision / PyTorch crash immed=
iately</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"413" data-end=3D"424">This means:</p>
<h1 data-start=3D"426" data-end=3D"498">=E2=9D=97 Your environment currentl=
y has <strong data-start=3D"461" data-end=3D"474">NumPy 2.x</strong>, which=
 is incompatible.</h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"500" data-end=3D"538">You <strong data-start=3D"508" data=
-end=3D"516">must</strong> install NumPy 1.26.x.</h3>
