<p data-start=3D"1152" data-end=3D"1211">For circuits between 4=E2=80=935M =
rows, EZKL setup typically needs:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1213" data-end=3D"1380">
<li data-start=3D"1213" data-end=3D"1236">
<p data-start=3D"1215" data-end=3D"1236"><strong data-start=3D"1215" data-e=
nd=3D"1236">16 GB RAM minimum</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1237" data-end=3D"1267">
<p data-start=3D"1239" data-end=3D"1267"><strong data-start=3D"1239" data-e=
nd=3D"1267">24=E2=80=9332 GB RAM recommended</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1268" data-end=3D"1380">
<p data-start=3D"1270" data-end=3D"1317">peak usage can reach <strong data-=
start=3D"1291" data-end=3D"1303">18=E2=80=9322 GB</strong> depending on:</p=
>
<ul data-start=3D"1320" data-end=3D"1380">
<li data-start=3D"1320" data-end=3D"1333">
<p data-start=3D"1322" data-end=3D"1333">decomp legs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1336" data-end=3D"1345">
<p data-start=3D"1338" data-end=3D"1345">logrows</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1348" data-end=3D"1362">
<p data-start=3D"1350" data-end=3D"1362">params scale</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1365" data-end=3D"1380">
<p data-start=3D"1367" data-end=3D"1380">lookup tables</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1382" data-end=3D"1410">So an AWS EC2 instance like:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1412" data-end=3D"1527">
<li data-start=3D"1412" data-end=3D"1442">
<p data-start=3D"1414" data-end=3D"1442"><strong data-start=3D"1414" data-e=
nd=3D"1440">m5.2xlarge (32 GB RAM)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1443" data-end=3D"1483">
<p data-start=3D"1445" data-end=3D"1483"><strong data-start=3D"1445" data-e=
nd=3D"1481">c5.2xlarge (16 GB RAM) with swap</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1484" data-end=3D"1527">
<p data-start=3D"1486" data-end=3D"1527"><strong data-start=3D"1486" data-e=
nd=3D"1527">r5.xlarge or r5.2xlarge (high memory)</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1529" data-end=3D"1539">will work.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1541" data-end=3D"1544">
<h1 data-start=3D"1546" data-end=3D"1651">=E2=AD=90 <strong data-start=3D"1=
550" data-end=3D"1651">Very important: Once the keys are created, they are =
small enough and your miner can run anywhere.</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"1653" data-end=3D"1737">You do NOT need a huge instance to=
