=3D"805">
Because SN2 scoring does <strong data-start=3D"830" data-end=3D"866">not ev=
aluate prediction accuracy</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"869" data-end=3D"895">SN2 validators only check:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"897" data-end=3D"1068">
<li data-start=3D"897" data-end=3D"921">
<p data-start=3D"899" data-end=3D"921">=E2=9C=94 your proofs verify</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"922" data-end=3D"974">
<p data-start=3D"924" data-end=3D"974">=E2=9C=94 your outputs match the exp=
ected ONNX structure</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"975" data-end=3D"1002">
<p data-start=3D"977" data-end=3D"1002">=E2=9C=94 your circuit is valid</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1003" data-end=3D"1032">
<p data-start=3D"1005" data-end=3D"1032">=E2=9C=94 your proof time is fast<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1033" data-end=3D"1068">
<p data-start=3D"1035" data-end=3D"1068">=E2=9C=94 your miner responds corr=
ectly</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1070" data-end=3D"1120"><strong data-start=3D"1070" data-e=
nd=3D"1120">They do NOT care whether the model is trained.</strong></p>
<hr data-start=3D"1122" data-end=3D"1125">
<h1 data-start=3D"1127" data-end=3D"1178">=F0=9F=9F=A2 <strong data-start=
=3D"1132" data-end=3D"1178">You SHOULD NOT retrain anything for Path B</str=
ong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"1180" data-end=3D"1192">By choosing:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"1194" data-end=3D"1245">
<p data-start=3D"1196" data-end=3D"1245">=F0=9F=9F=A7 Path B =E2=80=94 Rebu=
ild the exact SN2 reference model</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"1247" data-end=3D"1364">You are explicitly choosing <stron=
g data-start=3D"1275" data-end=3D"1282">not</strong> to use a trained CNN =
=E2=80=94<br data-start=3D"1305" data-end=3D"1308">
you are building the simple reference model to maximize:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1366" data-end=3D"1519">
<li data-start=3D"1366" data-end=3D"1388">
<p data-start=3D"1368" data-end=3D"1388">circuit simplicity</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1389" data-end=3D"1414">
<p data-start=3D"1391" data-end=3D"1414">smaller circuit sizes</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1415" data-end=3D"1433">
<p data-start=3D"1417" data-end=3D"1433">faster proving</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1434" data-end=3D"1459">
<p data-start=3D"1436" data-end=3D"1459">easier key generation</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1460" data-end=3D"1482">
<p data-start=3D"1462" data-end=3D"1482">lower memory usage</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1483" data-end=3D"1519">
<p data-start=3D"1485" data-end=3D"1519">guaranteed validator compatibility=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1521" data-end=3D"1551">If you train it, you will get:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1553" data-end=3D"1733">
<li data-start=3D"1553" data-end=3D"1587">
<p data-start=3D"1555" data-end=3D"1587">slightly different predictions</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1588" data-end=3D"1621">
<p data-start=3D"1590" data-end=3D"1621">but <strong data-start=3D"1594" da=
ta-end=3D"1619">no benefit in scoring</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1622" data-end=3D"1672">
<p data-start=3D"1624" data-end=3D"1672">bigger PK (because weights have mo=
re variance)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1673" data-end=3D"1691">
<p data-start=3D"1675" data-end=3D"1691">slower proving</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1692" data-end=3D"1733">
<p data-start=3D"1694" data-end=3D"1733">more chance of mismatch with valid=
ators</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1735" data-end=3D"1738">
<h1 data-start=3D"1740" data-end=3D"1806">=E2=9D=97 <strong data-start=3D"1=
744" data-end=3D"1806">VERY IMPORTANT: Training does NOT improve your SN2 r=
ewards</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"1808" data-end=3D"1833">SN2 rewards are based on:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1835" data-end=3D"1968">
<li data-start=3D"1835" data-end=3D"1845">
<p data-start=3D"1837" data-end=3D"1845">uptime</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1846" data-end=3D"1857">
<p data-start=3D"1848" data-end=3D"1857">latency</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1858" data-end=3D"1884">
<p data-start=3D"1860" data-end=3D"1884">proof generation speed</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1885" data-end=3D"1903">
<p data-start=3D"1887" data-end=3D"1903">proof validity</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1904" data-end=3D"1944">
<p data-start=3D"1906" data-end=3D"1944">responsiveness to validator reques=
ts</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1945" data-end=3D"1968">
<p data-start=3D"1947" data-end=3D"1968">circuit correctness</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1970" data-end=3D"1998"><strong data-start=3D"1970" data-e=
nd=3D"1998">Not prediction accuracy.</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"2000" data-end=3D"2109">All miners run using the same labe=
l extraction pipeline.<br data-start=3D"2056" data-end=3D"2059">
There is no "loss" or "metric" used by validators.</p>
