=F0=9F=91=89 <strong data-start=3D"245" data-end=3D"322">If we understand t=
he proof/validator logic, all the confusion disappears.</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"324" data-end=3D"378">Let=E2=80=99s reset.<br data-start=
=3D"336" data-end=3D"339">
Let=E2=80=99s rebuild the correct mental model.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"380" data-end=3D"383">
<h1 data-start=3D"385" data-end=3D"435">=F0=9F=9A=80 <strong data-start=3D"=
390" data-end=3D"435">FIRST: What determines SN2 miner scoring?</strong></h=
1>
<p data-start=3D"436" data-end=3D"489">SN2 miners are rewarded <strong data=
-start=3D"460" data-end=3D"467">NOT</strong> based on AI accuracy.</p>
<p data-start=3D"491" data-end=3D"518">They are rewarded based on:</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"520" data-end=3D"578"><strong data-start=3D"523" data-end=
=3D"578">1. Proof validity (must match expected ONNX schema)</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"579" data-end=3D"654">If your circuit=E2=80=99s outputs do=
 NOT match the validator=E2=80=99s expected ONNX model:</p>
<p data-start=3D"656" data-end=3D"743">=E2=9D=8C The validator rejects your=
 proof<br data-start=3D"690" data-end=3D"693">
=E2=9D=8C Your miner gets 0 score<br data-start=3D"718" data-end=3D"721">
=E2=9D=8C You lose emissions</p>
<p data-start=3D"745" data-end=3D"812">This is why the <strong data-start=
=3D"761" data-end=3D"811">output schema matters more than model training</s=
trong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"814" data-end=3D"817">
<h2 data-start=3D"819" data-end=3D"840"><strong data-start=3D"822" data-end=
=3D"840">2. Proof speed</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"841" data-end=3D"860">Validators measure:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"862" data-end=3D"928">
<li data-start=3D"862" data-end=3D"895">
<p data-start=3D"864" data-end=3D"895">how fast you generate a proof</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"896" data-end=3D"928">
<p data-start=3D"898" data-end=3D"928">how fast you answer requests</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"930" data-end=3D"952">Faster =E2=86=92 more rewards.</p>
<p data-start=3D"954" data-end=3D"1019">This is why simpler circuits (linea=
r models) outperform big CNNs.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1021" data-end=3D"1024">
<h2 data-start=3D"1026" data-end=3D"1059"><strong data-start=3D"1029" data-=
end=3D"1059">3. Uptime &amp; responsiveness</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"1060" data-end=3D"1129">If you return errors, timeouts, or=
 invalid proofs =E2=86=92 your score drops.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1131" data-end=3D"1134">
<h2 data-start=3D"1136" data-end=3D"1174"><strong data-start=3D"1139" data-=
end=3D"1174">4. No accuracy-based evaluation</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"1175" data-end=3D"1204">There is <strong data-start=3D"118=
4" data-end=3D"1192">zero</strong> reward for:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1206" data-end=3D"1315">
<li data-start=3D"1206" data-end=3D"1227">
<p data-start=3D"1208" data-end=3D"1227">model correctness</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1228" data-end=3D"1248">
<p data-start=3D"1230" data-end=3D"1248">good predictions</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1249" data-end=3D"1272">
<p data-start=3D"1251" data-end=3D"1272">good classification</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1273" data-end=3D"1315">
<p data-start=3D"1275" data-end=3D"1315">teacher-student knowledge distilla=
tion</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1317" data-end=3D"1340">Accuracy is irrelevant.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1342" data-end=3D"1345">
<h1 data-start=3D"1347" data-end=3D"1401">=F0=9F=A7=A9 <strong data-start=
=3D"1352" data-end=3D"1401">SECOND: What model does the validator expect?</=
strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"1402" data-end=3D"1418">This is the key.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1420" data-end=3D"1466">Validators do NOT accept arbitrar=
