</li>
<li data-start=3D"2252" data-end=3D"2269">
<p data-start=3D"2254" data-end=3D"2269">missing nonce</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2270" data-end=3D"2321">
<p data-start=3D"2272" data-end=3D"2321">wrong model (any difference from o=
fficial ONNX)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2322" data-end=3D"2344">
<p data-start=3D"2324" data-end=3D"2344">wrong quantization</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2345" data-end=3D"2366">
<p data-start=3D"2347" data-end=3D"2366">incorrect circuit</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2367" data-end=3D"2389">
<p data-start=3D"2369" data-end=3D"2389">too slow to return</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2391" data-end=3D"2464">Thus <strong data-start=3D"2396" d=
ata-end=3D"2463">your ONNX =E2=86=92 EZKL circuit must exactly match the re=
ference model</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2466" data-end=3D"2559">This is why training your own clas=
sifier (TinyAgeNet) failed =E2=80=94 it produced different outputs.</p>
