<p data-start=3D"2696" data-end=3D"2713">If your miner is:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2715" data-end=3D"2734">Fast (&lt; 150ms):</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2735" data-end=3D"2751">=E2=AD=90=E2=AD=90=E2=AD=90=E2=AD=
=90=E2=AD=90 high score</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2753" data-end=3D"2777">Medium (~300=E2=80=93800ms):</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2778" data-end=3D"2796">=E2=AD=90=E2=AD=90=E2=AD=90 modera=
te score</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2798" data-end=3D"2814">Slow (&gt; 1s):</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2815" data-end=3D"2826">=E2=AD=90 low score</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2828" data-end=3D"2846">Timeout (&gt; 4s)</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2847" data-end=3D"2904">=E2=9D=8C score =3D 0<br data-star=
t=3D"2858" data-end=3D"2861">
=E2=9D=8C may add penalties for repeated failures</p>
<p data-start=3D"2906" data-end=3D"2911">Thus:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2913" data-end=3D"3020">
<li data-start=3D"2913" data-end=3D"2934">
<p data-start=3D"2915" data-end=3D"2934">CPU circuits =3D slow</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2935" data-end=3D"2958">
<p data-start=3D"2937" data-end=3D"2958">large circuits =3D slow</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2959" data-end=3D"2978">
<p data-start=3D"2961" data-end=3D"2978">big pk.key =3D slow</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2979" data-end=3D"3020">
<p data-start=3D"2981" data-end=3D"3020">fast proofs =3D small models =3D h=
igh score</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3022" data-end=3D"3050">This is why most top miners:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3052" data-end=3D"3187">
<li data-start=3D"3052" data-end=3D"3079">
<p data-start=3D"3054" data-end=3D"3079">use a tiny linear model</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3080" data-end=3D"3091">
<p data-start=3D"3082" data-end=3D"3091">use GPU</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3092" data-end=3D"3139">
<p data-start=3D"3094" data-end=3D"3139">use hardware with high RAM (avoid =
swapping)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3140" data-end=3D"3187">
<p data-start=3D"3142" data-end=3D"3187">run ONNX graph that is intentional=
ly simple</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3189" data-end=3D"3192">
<h1 data-start=3D"3194" data-end=3D"3223">=F0=9F=94=81 <strong data-start=
=3D"3199" data-end=3D"3223">5. Consistency check</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"3225" data-end=3D"3247">Validators also check:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3249" data-end=3D"3393">
<li data-start=3D"3249" data-end=3D"3292">
<p data-start=3D"3251" data-end=3D"3292">if you consistently return valid p=
roofs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3293" data-end=3D"3337">
<p data-start=3D"3295" data-end=3D"3337">if your outputs match the expected=
 model</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3338" data-end=3D"3366">
<p data-start=3D"3340" data-end=3D"3366">if you use correct nonce</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3367" data-end=3D"3393">
<p data-start=3D"3369" data-end=3D"3393">if your uptime is stable</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3395" data-end=3D"3451">If you fail often =E2=86=92 your s=
core is reduced exponentially.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3453" data-end=3D"3456">
<h1 data-start=3D"3458" data-end=3D"3486">=F0=9F=93=89 <strong data-start=
=3D"3463" data-end=3D"3486">6. Negative scoring</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"3488" data-end=3D"3502">If your miner:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3504" data-end=3D"3612">
<li data-start=3D"3504" data-end=3D"3530">
<p data-start=3D"3506" data-end=3D"3530">returns invalid proofs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3531" data-end=3D"3550">
<p data-start=3D"3533" data-end=3D"3550">times out often</p>
