<p data-start=3D"318" data-end=3D"380">So the <strong data-start=3D"325" da=
ta-end=3D"359">baseline ONNX model <code data-start=3D"347" data-end=3D"357=
">age.onnx</code></strong> is expected to have:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"382" data-end=3D"542">
<li data-start=3D"382" data-end=3D"409">
<p data-start=3D"384" data-end=3D"409"><strong data-start=3D"384" data-end=
=3D"398">Input name</strong>: <code data-start=3D"400" data-end=3D"407">inp=
ut</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"410" data-end=3D"440">
<p data-start=3D"412" data-end=3D"440"><strong data-start=3D"412" data-end=
=3D"421">Dtype</strong>: <code data-start=3D"423" data-end=3D"432">float32<=
/code> (F32)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"441" data-end=3D"542">
<p data-start=3D"443" data-end=3D"472"><strong data-start=3D"443" data-end=
=3D"452">Shape</strong>: <code data-start=3D"454" data-end=3D"470">[1, 3, 6=
4, 64]</code></p>
<ul data-start=3D"475" data-end=3D"542">
<li data-start=3D"475" data-end=3D"488">
<p data-start=3D"477" data-end=3D"488">batch =3D 1</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"491" data-end=3D"507">
<p data-start=3D"493" data-end=3D"507">channels =3D 3</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"510" data-end=3D"525">
<p data-start=3D"512" data-end=3D"525">height =3D 64</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"528" data-end=3D"542">
<p data-start=3D"530" data-end=3D"542">width =3D 64</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"544" data-end=3D"632">This matches what you already used:<=
br data-start=3D"579" data-end=3D"582">
<code data-start=3D"582" data-end=3D"609">torch.randn(1, 3, 64, 64)</code> =
for export is correct.</p>
<p data-start=3D"634" data-end=3D"785">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F <strong data-star=
t=3D"637" data-end=3D"652">Nonce note:</strong><br data-start=3D"652" data-=
end=3D"655">
The competition config only describes the ML model schema.<br data-start=3D=
"713" data-end=3D"716">
The <strong data-start=3D"720" data-end=3D"742">custom-circuit doc</strong>=
 adds an extra requirement at the ZK level:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"787" data-end=3D"858">
<p data-start=3D"789" data-end=3D"858">One of the inputs to your circuit mu=
st be an F32 field named <code data-start=3D"850" data-end=3D"857">nonce</c=
ode>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"860" data-end=3D"875">So in practice:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"877" data-end=3D"974">
<li data-start=3D"877" data-end=3D"915">
<p data-start=3D"879" data-end=3D"915">ONNX baseline: input <code data-star=
t=3D"900" data-end=3D"907">input</code> (image)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"916" data-end=3D"974">
<p data-start=3D"918" data-end=3D"974">ZK circuit: inputs <code data-start=
=3D"937" data-end=3D"944">input</code> (image), <code data-start=3D"954" da=
ta-end=3D"961">nonce</code> (scalar F32)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"976" data-end=3D"1098">The nonce is <em data-start=3D"989"=
 data-end=3D"994">not</em> required as an ONNX input for the reference <cod=
e data-start=3D"1039" data-end=3D"1049">age.onnx</code>, but <strong data-s=
tart=3D"1055" data-end=3D"1070">is required</strong> in the EZKL circuit in=
puts.</p>
