<p data-start=3D"2438" data-end=3D"2637">The validator sometimes treats the=
 model output as a <strong data-start=3D"2491" data-end=3D"2521">flattened =
<code data-start=3D"2503" data-end=3D"2512">(1, 21)</code> vector</strong> =
for scoring/comparison, but it still expects the <strong data-start=3D"2571=
" data-end=3D"2585">ONNX graph</strong> to produce those 9 named outputs wi=
th those shapes.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2639" data-end=3D"2642">
<h2 data-start=3D"2644" data-end=3D"2682">3=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Why this sche=
ma matters so much</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2684" data-end=3D"2714">For your miner to be accepted:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2716" data-end=3D"2938">
<li data-start=3D"2716" data-end=3D"2778">
<p data-start=3D"2718" data-end=3D"2778">Your ONNX model <strong data-start=
=3D"2734" data-end=3D"2776">must have exactly these 9 output names</strong>=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2779" data-end=3D"2811">
<p data-start=3D"2781" data-end=3D"2811">And <strong data-start=3D"2785" da=
ta-end=3D"2809">exactly these shapes</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2812" data-end=3D"2872">
<p data-start=3D"2814" data-end=3D"2872">And the EZKL circuit must be compi=
led <strong data-start=3D"2852" data-end=3D"2870">from that ONNX</strong></=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2873" data-end=3D"2938">
<p data-start=3D"2875" data-end=3D"2938">And the proof must certify those o=
utputs for that input image</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2940" data-end=3D"2960">If you instead have:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2962" data-end=3D"3058">
<li data-start=3D"2962" data-end=3D"2999">
<p data-start=3D"2964" data-end=3D"2999">one output like <code data-start=
=3D"2980" data-end=3D"2997">logits: (1, 21)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3000" data-end=3D"3022">
<p data-start=3D"3002" data-end=3D"3022">or different names</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3023" data-end=3D"3058">
<p data-start=3D"3025" data-end=3D"3058">or missing any of the 9 outputs</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3060" data-end=3D"3065">then:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"3067" data-end=3D"3194">
<p data-start=3D"3069" data-end=3D"3194">=F0=9F=94=A5 The validator cannot =
match your outputs to the expected schema, so your proof / result is effect=
ively invalid for scoring.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"3196" data-end=3D"3366">This is <em data-start=3D"3204" da=
ta-end=3D"3213">exactly</em> why your TinyAgeNet student model (with a sing=
le <code data-start=3D"3263" data-end=3D"3272">(1, 21)</code> output) doesn=
=E2=80=99t fit the competition requirements, even though it=E2=80=99s a per=
fectly fine ML model.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3368" data-end=3D"3371">
<h2 data-start=3D"3373" data-end=3D"3419">4=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 How your SN2R=
eferenceModel should align</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3421" data-end=3D"3487">The SN2ReferenceModel (the simple =
linear model we discussed) must:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3489" data-end=3D"3805">
<li data-start=3D"3489" data-end=3D"3521">
<p data-start=3D"3491" data-end=3D"3521">Take <code data-start=3D"3496" dat=
a-end=3D"3519">input: (1, 3, 64, 64)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3522" data-end=3D"3586">
<p data-start=3D"3524" data-end=3D"3586">Optionally also take a <code data-=
start=3D"3547" data-end=3D"3554">nonce</code> argument for the EZKL circuit=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3587" data-end=3D"3648">
<p data-start=3D"3589" data-end=3D"3648">Produce <strong data-start=3D"3597=
" data-end=3D"3610">9 outputs</strong> with the exact names &amp; shapes ab=
ove</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3649" data-end=3D"3805">
<p data-start=3D"3651" data-end=3D"3690">Internally, it can do something si=
mple:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3693" data-end=3D"3805">
<li data-start=3D"3693" data-end=3D"3731">
<p data-start=3D"3695" data-end=3D"3731">mean-pool the image =E2=86=92 tens=
or <code data-start=3D"3724" data-end=3D"3731">(1,3)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3734" data-end=3D"3759">
<p data-start=3D"3736" data-end=3D"3759">linear layer =E2=86=92 <code data-=
start=3D"3751" data-end=3D"3759">(1,21)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3762" data-end=3D"3805">
<p data-start=3D"3764" data-end=3D"3805">slice into the 9 chunks as per the=
 schema</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3807" data-end=3D"3875">The validator does <strong data-st=
art=3D"3826" data-end=3D"3833">not</strong> care what math you do inside, a=
s long as:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3877" data-end=3D"4000">
<li data-start=3D"3877" data-end=3D"3903">
<p data-start=3D"3879" data-end=3D"3903">ONNX structure matches</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3904" data-end=3D"3936">
<p data-start=3D"3906" data-end=3D"3936">the circuit matches the ONNX</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3937" data-end=3D"3959">
<p data-start=3D"3939" data-end=3D"3959">the proof is valid</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3960" data-end=3D"4000">
<p data-start=3D"3962" data-end=3D"4000">the outputs have correct shapes/na=
mes.</p>
