<p data-start=3D"3573" data-end=3D"3628">Just <strong data-start=3D"3578" d=
ata-end=3D"3606">match the reference ONNX</strong> and make fast proofs.</p=
>
<hr data-start=3D"3630" data-end=3D"3633">
<h1 data-start=3D"3635" data-end=3D"3680">=F0=9F=A7=A9 <strong data-start=
=3D"3640" data-end=3D"3680">Your confusion before was reasonable</strong></=
h1>
<p data-start=3D"3682" data-end=3D"3720">You thought the competition was ab=
out:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3722" data-end=3D"3806">
<li data-start=3D"3722" data-end=3D"3734">
<p data-start=3D"3724" data-end=3D"3734">accuracy</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3735" data-end=3D"3752">
<p data-start=3D"3737" data-end=3D"3752">better models</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3753" data-end=3D"3782">
<p data-start=3D"3755" data-end=3D"3782">improved student networks</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3783" data-end=3D"3806">
<p data-start=3D"3785" data-end=3D"3806">better ML performance</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3808" data-end=3D"3843">That makes sense in traditional ML=
.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3845" data-end=3D"3922">But SN2 is <strong data-start=3D"3=
856" data-end=3D"3877">not an ML contest</strong>.<br data-start=3D"3878" d=
ata-end=3D"3881">
It is a <strong data-start=3D"3889" data-end=3D"3921">ZK proof performance =
contest</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3924" data-end=3D"3927">
<h1 data-start=3D"3929" data-end=3D"3948">=F0=9F=8F=81 <strong data-start=
=3D"3934" data-end=3D"3948">Conclusion</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"3950" data-end=3D"3997">You should NOT train SN2ReferenceM=
odel because:</p>
<p data-start=3D"3999" data-end=3D"4255">=E2=9C=94 Training changes weights=
<br data-start=3D"4025" data-end=3D"4028">
=E2=9C=94 Changing weights changes outputs<br data-start=3D"4062" data-end=
=3D"4065">
=E2=9C=94 Changing outputs breaks validity<br data-start=3D"4099" data-end=
=3D"4102">
=E2=9C=94 Validator rejects non-matching models<br data-start=3D"4141" data=
-end=3D"4144">
=E2=9C=94 SN2 is testing ZK proving speed, not ML accuracy<br data-start=3D=
"4194" data-end=3D"4197">
=E2=9C=94 The reference model exists only to be reproduced exactly</p>
