-start=3D"194" data-end=3D"220">single, clean pipeline</strong> you can run=
 end-to-end.</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"246" data-end=3D"681">
<p data-start=3D"248" data-end=3D"495">=F0=9F=A7=A0 Note on <code data-star=
t=3D"259" data-end=3D"266">nonce</code>:<br data-start=3D"267" data-end=3D"=
270">
The <em data-start=3D"276" data-end=3D"290">general docs</em> talk about a =
<code data-start=3D"304" data-end=3D"311">nonce</code> input for custom cir=
cuits,<br data-start=3D"338" data-end=3D"341">
but the <strong data-start=3D"351" data-end=3D"388">SN2 competition 1 refer=
ence model</strong> (<code data-start=3D"390" data-end=3D"400">age.onnx</co=
de> via <code data-start=3D"405" data-end=3D"436">create_competition_circui=
t.py</code>) only has <strong data-start=3D"447" data-end=3D"460">one input=
</strong>: the image <code data-start=3D"472" data-end=3D"492">input: [1,3,=
64,64]</code>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"502" data-end=3D"681">For this competition path, we=E2=80=
=99ll <strong data-start=3D"535" data-end=3D"557">match that exactly</stron=
g>:<br data-start=3D"558" data-end=3D"561">
<strong data-start=3D"563" data-end=3D"614">no <code data-start=3D"568" dat=
a-end=3D"575">nonce</code> input in ONNX, just the image input.</strong><br=
 data-start=3D"614" data-end=3D"617">
This keeps us <strong data-start=3D"633" data-end=3D"680">identical to the =
validator=E2=80=99s expected model</strong>.</p>
