<p data-start=3D"1182" data-end=3D"1197">The key phrase:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"1199" data-end=3D"1270">
<p data-start=3D"1201" data-end=3D"1270">"One of the inputs to your circuit=
 must be an F32 field named nonce."</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"1272" data-end=3D"1283">This means:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1285" data-end=3D"1416">
<li data-start=3D"1285" data-end=3D"1332">
<p data-start=3D"1287" data-end=3D"1332">The <strong data-start=3D"1291" da=
ta-end=3D"1307">EZKL circuit</strong> (your proving circuit)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1333" data-end=3D"1364">
<p data-start=3D"1335" data-end=3D"1364">Must accept a <code data-start=3D"=
1349" data-end=3D"1356">nonce</code> input</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1365" data-end=3D"1416">
<p data-start=3D"1367" data-end=3D"1416">Even if the <strong data-start=3D"=
1379" data-end=3D"1416">ONNX model itself does not use it</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1418" data-end=3D"1436">This is important:</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"1438" data-end=3D"1474">=E2=9E=A4 <strong data-start=3D"1=
443" data-end=3D"1472">Nonce is NOT part of ONNX</strong></h2>
<h2 data-start=3D"1475" data-end=3D"1524">=E2=9E=A4 <strong data-start=3D"1=
480" data-end=3D"1522">Nonce IS part of the ZK circuit inputs</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"1526" data-end=3D"1541">In other words:</p>
<p data-start=3D"1543" data-end=3D"1561"><strong data-start=3D"1543" data-e=
nd=3D"1561">ONNX receives:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1562" data-end=3D"1585">
<li data-start=3D"1562" data-end=3D"1585">
<p data-start=3D"1564" data-end=3D"1585"><code data-start=3D"1564" data-end=
=3D"1571">input</code>  (image only)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1587" data-end=3D"1613"><strong data-start=3D"1587" data-e=
nd=3D"1613">EZKL circuit receives:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1614" data-end=3D"1633">
<li data-start=3D"1614" data-end=3D"1623">
<p data-start=3D"1616" data-end=3D"1623"><code data-start=3D"1616" data-end=
=3D"1623">input</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1624" data-end=3D"1633">
<p data-start=3D"1626" data-end=3D"1633"><code data-start=3D"1626" data-end=
=3D"1633">nonce</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1635" data-end=3D"1718">Even though ONNX doesn't use nonce=
, the circuit MUST allow it for security reasons.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1720" data-end=3D"1723">
<h1 data-start=3D"1725" data-end=3D"1777">=F0=9F=92=A1 So why did I omit no=
nce from the ONNX export?</h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"1778" data-end=3D"1859">=F0=9F=91=89 Because the ONNX mod=
el must exactly match the validator=E2=80=99s reference model.</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1861" data-end=3D"2002">
<li data-start=3D"1861" data-end=3D"1907">
<p data-start=3D"1863" data-end=3D"1907">Validators load <strong data-start=
=3D"1879" data-end=3D"1893">their copy</strong> of <code data-start=3D"1897=
" data-end=3D"1907">age.onnx</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1908" data-end=3D"1960">
<p data-start=3D"1910" data-end=3D"1960">They compute expected outputs usin=
g that ONNX file</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1961" data-end=3D"2002">
<p data-start=3D"1963" data-end=3D"2002">Your ONNX must match theirs <em da=
ta-start=3D"1991" data-end=3D"2002">precisely</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2004" data-end=3D"2034">If we include <code data-start=3D"=
2018" data-end=3D"2025">nonce</code> in ONNX:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2036" data-end=3D"2200">
<li data-start=3D"2036" data-end=3D"2070">
<p data-start=3D"2038" data-end=3D"2070">ONNX input schema would differ</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2071" data-end=3D"2107">
<p data-start=3D"2073" data-end=3D"2107">Validator cannot load your model</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2108" data-end=3D"2148">
<p data-start=3D"2110" data-end=3D"2148">Validator computes different resul=
ts</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2149" data-end=3D"2174">
<p data-start=3D"2151" data-end=3D"2174">Proof becomes invalid</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2175" data-end=3D"2200">
<p data-start=3D"2177" data-end=3D"2200">Miner =E2=86=92 score =3D <strong =
data-start=3D"2193" data-end=3D"2198">0</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2202" data-end=3D"2246">That is why ONNX <strong data-star=
t=3D"2219" data-end=3D"2245">must not include nonce</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2248" data-end=3D"2251">
<h1 data-start=3D"2253" data-end=3D"2283">=F0=9F=92=A1 Then where is nonce =
used?</h1>
