<p data-start=3D"303" data-end=3D"341">This one line explains <strong data-=
start=3D"326" data-end=3D"340">everything</strong>:</p>
<hr data-start=3D"343" data-end=3D"346">
<h1 data-start=3D"348" data-end=3D"408">=F0=9F=9A=A8 <strong data-start=3D"=
353" data-end=3D"406">1. New circuits must beat the existing best by 2%</st=
rong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"409" data-end=3D"420">This means:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"422" data-end=3D"631">
<li data-start=3D"422" data-end=3D"468">
<p data-start=3D"424" data-end=3D"468">If today the SOTA circuit has score =
=3D 1.00</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"469" data-end=3D"507">
<p data-start=3D"471" data-end=3D"507">Your circuit must score <strong data=
-start=3D"495" data-end=3D"505">&gt; 1.02</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"508" data-end=3D"550">
<p data-start=3D"510" data-end=3D"550">Otherwise you get <strong data-start=
=3D"528" data-end=3D"548">no =E2=80=9CSOTA reward=E2=80=9D</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"551" data-end=3D"631">
<p data-start=3D"553" data-end=3D"631">And your circuit will <strong data-s=
tart=3D"575" data-end=3D"590">not replace</strong> the SOTA circuit stored =
by the validator</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"633" data-end=3D"719">This is <em data-start=3D"641" data-=
end=3D"650">exactly</em> what the community guy was complaining about =E2=
=80=94 and they are correct.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"721" data-end=3D"772">=E2=9C=94 Older miners have their c=
ircuit =E2=80=9Clocked in=E2=80=9D</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"773" data-end=3D"860">=E2=9C=94 New miners need to break =
into the leaderboard by beating the existing top by 2%</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"861" data-end=3D"930">=E2=9C=94 That 2% threshold is <str=
ong data-start=3D"888" data-end=3D"896">hard</strong>, because noise &amp; =
variance exist</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"931" data-end=3D"979">=E2=9C=94 So new miners feel =E2=80=
=9Clocked out=E2=80=9D early on</h3>
<p data-start=3D"981" data-end=3D"1043">This is not a theory =E2=80=94 it=
=E2=80=99s literally how the subnet is coded.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1045" data-end=3D"1048">
