<hr data-start=3D"3384" data-end=3D"3387">
<h1 data-start=3D"3389" data-end=3D"3431">=F0=9F=94=A5 STRATEGY 5 =E2=80=94=
 Minimize Python overhead</h1>
<p data-start=3D"3433" data-end=3D"3495">A single slow Python GC pause is e=
nough to ruin your SOTA run.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3497" data-end=3D"3506">You must:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3508" data-end=3D"3544">=E2=9C=94 Use PyPy or Python GC t=
uning</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"3545" data-end=3D"3599">=E2=9C=94 Avoid allocating tensor=
s inside inference loop</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"3600" data-end=3D"3634">=E2=9C=94 Preload EZKL runtime st=
ate</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"3635" data-end=3D"3672">=E2=9C=94 Cache witness &amp; inp=
ut objects</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"3673" data-end=3D"3722">=E2=9C=94 Avoid reloading the cir=
cuit for each call</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"3723" data-end=3D"3773">=E2=9C=94 Use async worker thread=
s to avoid blocking</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3775" data-end=3D"3841">Top miners keep their Python loop =
=E2=80=9Chot=E2=80=9D and extremely lightweight.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3843" data-end=3D"3846">
<h1 data-start=3D"3848" data-end=3D"3907">=F0=9F=94=A5 STRATEGY 6 =E2=80=94=
 Pre-generate proving key &amp; load it in RAM</h1>
<p data-start=3D"3909" data-end=3D"3936">Disk I/O kills performance.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3938" data-end=3D"3983">The PK is HUGE (e.g., 5=E2=80=9312=
 GB).<br data-start=3D"3969" data-end=3D"3972">
Top miners:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3985" data-end=3D"4120">
<li data-start=3D"3985" data-end=3D"4005">
<p data-start=3D"3987" data-end=3D"4005">load PK into RAM</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4006" data-end=3D"4024">
<p data-start=3D"4008" data-end=3D"4024">keep it pinned</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4025" data-end=3D"4056">
<p data-start=3D"4027" data-end=3D"4056">avoid loading it repeatedly</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4057" data-end=3D"4120">
<p data-start=3D"4059" data-end=3D"4120">use tmpfs (<code data-start=3D"407=
0" data-end=3D"4080">/dev/shm</code>) to store circuit/PK for ultra-fast I/=
O</p>
</li>
</ul>
